IMPORTANT: After completing the task below, you MUST output ONLY a raw JSON object. Do NOT wrap it in markdown or add any prose — the workflow fails without it.

Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Act as a senior product strategist and release planner. For this exact MSW repository, produce an exhaustive capability matrix for a native macOS 26 menu-bar app, then prioritize a coherent first shippable release and later phases without losing important safety boundaries. Include installation/bootstrap, all three workspace lifecycle controls, metrics/logs, repositories, ports/tunnels, GitHub auth, host-only pushes, disk/resources, maintenance, backups/restores, diagnostics, settings, update strategy, and terminal escape hatches. Explain what the app can automate safely, what requires typed confirmation, and what must remain a deliberate advanced workflow. Return user stories, success criteria, migration stages, and measurable verification milestones. Do not edit files, run project-wide tests, formatters, or linters.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

